[{"category":"section","location":"theory/#Theory","page":"Theory","text":"<!– The Delaunay Tessellation Field Estimator (DTFE) and its extension to phase space (PS-DTFE) are mathematical tools for the reconstruction of the density and velocity field of a discrete point set. We review here the derivations underlying these reconstruction methods. –>\n\nnabla rho = \nbeginpmatrix\np_l_1-p_l_0\nvdots\np_l_d-p_l_0\nendpmatrix^-1\nbeginpmatrix\nrho_1-rho_0\nvdots\nrho_d-rho_0\nendpmatrix","title":"Theory"},{"category":"section","location":"citations/#Citations","page":"Citations","text":"<!– This code accompanies the publication Phase-Space Delaunay Tessellation Field Estimator, Job Feldbrugge, 2024. When using the code in your work, please cite both the paper and the code: –>\n\n<!-- @article{Feldbrugge2024,\n    author = {Feldbrugge, Job},\n    title = {Phase-space Delaunay tessellation field estimator},\n    journal = {Monthly Notices of the Royal Astronomical Society},\n    volume = {536},\n    number = {1},\n    pages = {807-815},\n    year = {2024},\n    month = {12},\n    issn = {0035-8711},\n    doi = {10.1093/mnras/stae2627},\n    url = {https://doi.org/10.1093/mnras/stae2627},\n    eprint = {https://academic.oup.com/mnras/article-pdf/536/1/807/61019429/stae2627.pdf},\n} -->\n\n<!-- @misc{FeldbruggeHertzsch2025,\n  author = {Feldbrugge, Job},\n  title = {Nbody2D.jl -- Julia implementation of the Phase-Space Delaunay Tessellation Field Estimator},\n  year = {2025},\n  month = {aug},\n  doi = {10.5281/zenodo.16637561},\n  url = {http://dx.doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.16637561}\n} -->\n\nPlease also consider citing the following papers that have been foundational to the development of the Nbody2D:\n\n<!– * Delaunay Tessellation Field Estimator: \n\nContinuous fields and discrete samples: reconstruction through Delaunay tessellations, by W.E. Schaap and R. van de Weygaert, 2000, \nThe PhD thesis of W.E. Schaap, 2007, University of Groningen, Netherlands –>","title":"Citations"},{"category":"section","location":"reference/#Reference","page":"Reference","text":"","title":"Reference"},{"category":"module","location":"reference/#Nbody2D.Nbody2D","page":"Reference","text":"A simple two-dimensional cosmological N-body code.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Nbody2D.Nbody2D"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/#Nbody2D.Box","page":"Reference","text":"The cosmological box, setting the volume of the box L^3 and the number of particles N^3.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Nbody2D.Box"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/#Nbody2D.Cosmology","page":"Reference","text":"The cosmological background in which the N-body simulation runs with the current Hubble rate H0, the matter density OmegaM, dark energy density OmegaL and the curvature component OmegaK.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Nbody2D.Cosmology"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/#Nbody2D.State","page":"Reference","text":"The state of the N-body simulation in phase-space.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Nbody2D.State"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#Nbody2D.CIC-Tuple{Any, Box}","page":"Reference","text":"Cloud-in-Cell density estimator.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Nbody2D.CIC"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#Nbody2D.Drift-Tuple{Any, Any, Any, Cosmology}","page":"Reference","text":"A drift step.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Nbody2D.Drift"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#Nbody2D.GRF-Tuple{Any, Any, Any, Any, Box}","page":"Reference","text":"Generate an unconstrained Gaussian random field.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Nbody2D.GRF"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#Nbody2D.Interp2D-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"Two dimensional interpolation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Nbody2D.Interp2D"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#Nbody2D.Kick-Tuple{Any, Any, Any, Box, Any, Cosmology}","page":"Reference","text":"A kick step.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Nbody2D.Kick"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#Nbody2D.LeapFrog-Tuple{Any, Any, Any, Any, Box, Cosmology}","page":"Reference","text":"The Leap Frog integrator.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Nbody2D.LeapFrog"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#Nbody2D.Zeldovich-Tuple{Any, Any, Any, Box, Cosmology}","page":"Reference","text":"Evaluate the Zel'dovich approximation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Nbody2D.Zeldovich"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#Nbody2D.adot-Tuple{Any, Cosmology}","page":"Reference","text":"The derivative of the scale factor.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Nbody2D.adot"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#Nbody2D.growing_mode-Tuple{AbstractFloat, Cosmology}","page":"Reference","text":"The growing mode.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Nbody2D.growing_mode"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#Nbody2D.growing_mode-Tuple{Vector, Cosmology}","page":"Reference","text":"The growing mode.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Nbody2D.growing_mode"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#Nbody2D.growing_mode_norm-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"The normalization of the growing mode.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Nbody2D.growing_mode_norm"},{"category":"section","location":"#Nbody2D","page":"Home","text":"Documentation for Nbody2D.\n\n(Image: Density field)","title":"Nbody2D"},{"category":"section","location":"#Installation","page":"Home","text":"The Nbody2D package can be installed with the Julia package manager. From the Julia REPL, type ] to enter the Pkg REPL mode and run:\n\npkg> add Nbody2D\n\nOr, equivalently, via the Pkg API:\n\njulia> import Pkg; Pkg.add(\"Nbody2D\")","title":"Installation"},{"category":"section","location":"#Usage","page":"Home","text":"<!– Given the initial (coords_q) and final (coords_x) particle positions and velocities vels of an N-body simulation, we estimate the density, velocity and number of streams fields as follows: –>\n\nusing Nbody2D\n\nm       = 1.  # particle mass\n# depth   = 5\n# sim_box = SimBox(L, Ni)\n\n# ps_dtfe_sb = ps_dtfe_subbox(coords_q, coords_x, vels, m, depth, sim_box)\n\n# Range      = 0.:0.2:100.\n# coords_arr = [[L/2., y, z] for y in Range, z in Range]\n# density_field  = density_subbox(coords_arr, ps_dtfe_sb)\n# nstreams_field = numberOfStreams_subbox(coords_arr, ps_dtfe_sb)\n# velocity_field = velocitySum_subbox(coords_arr, ps_dtfe_sb)\n\n<!– Please have a look at the Tutorial page for more details. –>","title":"Usage"},{"category":"section","location":"#Contributors","page":"Home","text":"This code was written by:\n\nJob Feldbrugge (job.feldbrugge@ed.ac.uk)\n\n<!– * Benjamin Hertzsch (benjamin.hertzsch@ed.ac.uk) –>","title":"Contributors"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorial/#Tutorial","page":"Tutorial","text":"In this tutorial, we demonstrate the usage of the Nbody2D.jl ","title":"Tutorial"}]
